{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-19-1","title":"Jeremiah 19:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Under the type of breaking a potter's vessel, is foreshewn the desolation of the Jews for their sins.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3397. B.C. 607. Go. 10,11; 18:2-4; 32:14; Isa 30:14; *marg: La 4:2; 2Co 4:7 the ancients of the people. 26:17; Nu 11:16; 1Ch 24:4-6; Eze 8:11,12; 9:6; Mt 26:3; 27:1,41,42 Ac 4:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-2","title":"Jeremiah 19:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the valley. 7:31,32; 32:35; Jos 15:8; 2Ki 23:10; 2Ch 28:3; 33:6 east-gate. Heb. sun-gate. Ne 3:29 and proclaim. 1:7; 3:12; 7:2; 11:6; 26:2; Pr 1:20-22; Eze 3:10,11; Jon 3:2 Mt 10:27; Ac 5:20; 20:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-3","title":"Jeremiah 19:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Hear. 13:18; 17:20; Ps 2:10; 102:15; 110:5; Mt 10:18; Re 2:29 his ears. 1Sa 3:11; 4:16-18; 2Ki 21:12,13; Isa 28:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-4","title":"Jeremiah 19:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>they have. 2:13,17,19,34; 5:6; 15:6; 16:11; 17:13; De 28:20; 31:16-18 De 32:15-23; 2Ki 22:16,17; Isa 65:11; Da 9:5-15 estranged. 2Ki 21:4,5,7; 23:11,12; 2Ch 33:4-7 burned. 7:9; 11:13; 18:15; 32:29-35; De 13:6,13; 28:36,64; 32:17 filled. 2:30,34; 7:31,32; 22:17; 26:15,23; 2Ki 21:6,16; 24:4; Isa 59:7 La 4:13; Mt 23:34,35; Lu 11:50; Re 16:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-5","title":"Jeremiah 19:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>the high. Nu 22:41 to burn. 7:31; De 12:31; 2Ki 17:17; 2Ch 28:3; Ps 106:37,38; Eze 16:20,21 Eze 20:26 which. 7:31,32; 32:35; Le 18:21 neither. Eze 38:10; Da 2:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-6","title":"Jeremiah 19:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>this. 2,11; 7:32,33; Jos 15:8; Isa 30:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-7","title":"Jeremiah 19:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I will make. Job 5:12,13; Ps 33:10,11; Pr 21:30; Isa 8:10; 28:17,18; 30:1-3 La 3:37; Ro 3:31; 4:14 I will cause. 9:21; 15:2,9; 18:21; 22:25; 46:26; Le 26:17; De 28:25 and their. 7:33; 8:2; 9:22; 16:4; 22:19; 34:20; De 28:26; Ps 79:2,3; Re 19:18-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-8","title":"Jeremiah 19:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>9:9-11; 18:16; 25:18; 49:13; 50:13; Le 26:32; 1Ki 9:8; 2Ch 7:20,21 La 2:15,16; Zep 2:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-9","title":"Jeremiah 19:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>eat the. Le 26:29; De 28:53-57; 2Ki 6:26-29; Isa 9:20; La 2:20; 4:10 Eze 5:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-10","title":"Jeremiah 19:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>48:12; 51:63,64</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-11","title":"Jeremiah 19:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Even. 13:14; Ps 2:9; Isa 30:14; La 4:2; Re 2:27 made whole. Heb. healed. bury. 6; 7:31,32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-12","title":"Jeremiah 19:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>make. lit. give. Jer 10:13; 11:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-13","title":"Jeremiah 19:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>defiled. 2Ki 23:10,12,14; Ps 74:7; 79:1; Eze 7:21,22 upon. 32:29; 2Ki 23:12; Zep 1:5 have poured. 7:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-14","title":"Jeremiah 19:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>from. 2,3 he stood. 17:19; 26:2; 2Ch 20:5; 24:20,21; Lu 21:37,38; Ac 5:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-19-15","title":"Jeremiah 19:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>because. 7:26; 17:23; 35:15-17; 2Ch 36:16,17; Ne 9:17,29; Zec 7:11-14 Ac 7:51,52 hardened.This is a metaphor taken from unruly and unbroken oxen, who resist the yoke, and break and run away with their gears.</p>\n<p>that they. Ps 58:2-5</p>"}]}